{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI evidence for Gerrit change 2133 patchset 1. GitHub run 32605850360 completed with failure. All four matrix environments reported one deterministic failure in tests/unit/test_snapshot_docs.py::test_hmac_trust_model_documented. The contract was introduced before ADR 0049 and still requires the legacy HMAC-SHA256 name, its lack of non-repudiation, and the current in-toto and DSSE shape. Investigation confirmed that ADR 0049 and the HMAC removal migration superseded HMAC for current operation certificates, while F09 retains accurate legacy compatibility guidance within docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md. The document now states that pre-migration gate records used HMAC-SHA256, that symmetric verification conferred forging power and no non-repudiation, and that these readable records return unknown_scheme and cannot certify a current gated operation. Focused verification passed. The snapshot documentation contract passed with 1 test, the reuse-surface contract passed with 4 tests, the signing lifecycle contract passed with 23 tests, the documentation index check passed, and git diff --check passed. The full suite was not run locally under the approved reduced policy."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787444192890587001,"uuid":"453f9b39-ed42-41fc-a12e-9ed1e0f9bf58"}